# 2. Stack Using Array

###  Problem Statement

Create a stack of size `M` using an array and perform stack operations such as initialization, checking empty/full conditions, insertion, deletion, peek, and display.

###  Approach

1. Define the stack using `typedef struct stacktype`.
2. Store the elements in an array.
3. Use `top` to keep track of the top element.
4. Initialize `top` to `-1` using `initstack()`.
5. Insert elements using `newel()`.
6. Remove elements using `delel()`.
7. Check the top element using `peek()`.
8. Display the stack using `display()`.

###  Modular Functions

```text
initstack()
     ↓
newel()
     ↓
delel()
     ↓
peek()
     ↓
isempty()
     ↓
isfull()
     ↓
display()
```

###  Example

```text
Stack:
10 20 30 40 50
             ↑
            TOP

Peek = 50
```

### ⏱️ Complexity

| Operation | Time Complexity |
| --------- | --------------: |
| Push      |            O(1) |
| Pop       |            O(1) |
| Peek      |            O(1) |
| isEmpty   |            O(1) |
| isFull    |            O(1) |
| Display   |            O(n) |



